.TH STARTUPSOUND-MX 1 "2026-08-30" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
startupsound-mx \- play the configured MX login sound at session startup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B startupsound-mx
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B startupsound-mx
is invoked automatically as an Xfce autostart entry. It waits for the
session's sound server and for
.B xfce4-session
to finish starting, then plays either the user's custom login sound or
the current sound theme's default login sound, depending on the
preferences set in
.BR mx-system-sounds (1).
.PP
If login sounds are disabled, or no configuration is present, the
script exits without playing anything.
.SH OPTIONS
This script takes no command-line options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/MX-Linux/mx-system-sounds/mx-login-logout_sounds.conf
Whether the login sound is enabled.
.TP
.I ~/.config/MX-Linux/mx-system-sounds/startupsound.conf
Path to the custom login sound, if one is set.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/zstartup-sound.desktop
Autostart entry that runs this script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mx-system-sounds (1)
